# `npm run dev -- --mode stub` — the back-office measured against a FAKE backend.
#
# The admin portal is verified in the browser rather than by unit tests (PO ruling for this phase),
# and several of its states cannot be produced against a real service without real credentials or a
# damaged database: a signed-out session, a dead session, a VIEWER, a 503. The stub answers all of
# them on :3301 and is driven over HTTP, so a scenario is one curl away.
#
# ⚠️ NEVER POINT THIS AT A REAL BACKEND. `--mode stub` also runs on a second port so the ordinary
# dev server on :2200 keeps talking to :3300 untouched.
#
# No secrets here, which is why this file is committed while `.env.local` is not.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3301

# The server answering :3301 is `tests/stubs/stub-server.mjs` — start it with `npm run stub`.
